    q: "Why is my Follett ice machine not making ice?",
    a: "A Follett ice machine that stopped making ice usually comes down to one of three things: an auger drive gear motor failure (the auger is the mechanical heart of Chewblet chewable ice production and the most common Follett failure at year 5 to 8 typical), a water-side fault (closed inlet, scaled inlet valve, clogged supply filter), or a control board issue (more common on older Symphony Plus dispensers at year 8 to 12). Our techs at Same Day Appliance Repair work the diagnostic cheapest-first because about 4 in 5 Follett no-production calls in LA, OC, Ventura, and the Inland Empire land on auger drive or water-side issues before sealed-system work is needed. $120 commercial diagnostic, applied toward repair."
