    q: "How long does a Follett ice machine repair take?",
    a: "Time-to-restoration depends on the failure category. Cleaning service (Sanitizer 2.0 cycle on Symphony Plus): 60 to 90 minutes, same-day. Water filter replacement: 30 to 60 minutes, same-day. Dispense valve actuator (Symphony Plus / Maestro Plus): 60 to 90 minutes on-site, same-day. Auger gear motor (Chewblet 7Series, 25Series, Ice Pro): 90 to 120 minutes, same-day if on truck. Symphony Plus control board: same-day if on truck (2 to 3 hours) or 3 to 5 day Easton PA standard ship. Refrigerant work (EPA 608): 3 to 5 hours, usually same-day. Compressor: full day plus often next-day completion. Less common Follett parts (older Symphony control boards, specialty Chewblet auger flights) can take 1 to 2 weeks on backorder — we pre-confirm parts availability at diagnostic."
  },
  {
    q: "How much does Follett ice machine repair cost?",
    a: "Diagnostic visit $120, waived with repair. Typical repair line items: cleaning service plus Sanitizer 2.0 cycle $200 to $340; water filter $80 to $180; water inlet valve $260 to $420; dispense valve actuator (Symphony Plus / Maestro Plus) $245 to $385; auger gear motor (Chewblet) $385 to $625; UV bulb replacement (Symphony Plus UV-equipped) $140 to $240; condenser fan motor $300 to $520; Symphony Plus control board $485 to $785; refrigerant leak repair plus recharge $700 to $1,500; compressor replacement (countertop and undercounter) $1,200 to $2,000; compressor replacement (modular) $1,600 to $2,400. Most healthcare-facility calls resolve in the $245 to $625 range when the symptom points to dispense valve, auger gear motor, or sensor work."
