<section class="section">
  <div class="container narrow">
    <p class="section-number">Production-failure diagnostic</p>
    <h2>A Follett that stopped making ice has auger-side, water-side, or refrigerant-side root cause. Three-step order, cheapest first.</h2>

    <p>A Follett ice machine that stopped making ice usually comes down to one of three things: an auger drive gear motor failure (the auger is the mechanical heart of Chewblet chewable ice production and the most common Follett service item — year 5 to 8 typical wear, $385 to $625 replacement), a water-side fault (closed inlet, scaled inlet valve, clogged supply filter), or a control board issue (more common on older Symphony Plus dispensers at year 8 to 12, $485 to $785 replacement). Follett is an independent Pennsylvania manufacturer (Easton PA, founded 1948, family-owned) — different parts network and component design from Welbilt (Manitowoc), Ali Group (Scotsman, Ice-O-Matic), or Hoshizaki Corporation. Our techs at Same Day Appliance Repair work the diagnostic cheapest-first because about 4 in 5 Follett no-production calls in LA, OC, Ventura, and the Inland Empire land on auger drive or water-side issues before sealed-system work is needed.</p>

    <p>Across LA County, our Follett service calls come from a predictable mix of operations: Cedars-Sinai outpatient clinics with Symphony Plus dispensers on hospital floors, UCLA Medical Center facilities running Symphony Plus across patient care wings, Kaiser locations across LA and Orange County with Symphony Plus standardized for staff and visitor service, dialysis centers where Symphony Plus is the specified dispenser for patient hydration, higher-end LA restaurants and hotel pool bars with Maestro Plus dispensing Chewblet ice as part of a premium beverage value proposition, and dental offices plus executive suites with 7Series and 25Series compact countertop Chewblet machines.</p>

    <p>$120 commercial diagnostic, waived with repair. BHGS #A49573 + EPA 608 Universal #1346255700410 for sealed-system work. Follett Easton PA parts network access (3 to 5 day standard ship, 1 to 3 day expedite available). Common Chewblet auger gear motors and Symphony Plus dispense valve actuators on the truck.</p>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="section section-gray">
  <div class="container">
    <p class="section-number">Diagnostic approaches by product line</p>
    <h2>Three diagnostic methods across the Follett lineup.</h2>

    <p>Follett ships three meaningfully different product architectures across its current lineup. The right read-first approach changes with the line. Our techs at Same Day Appliance Repair identify the line by serial number on the phone before dispatch so the right tools and reference manuals are on the truck.</p>

    <h3 class="series-h3">7Series and 25Series Chewblet — auger drive amp draw measurement</h3>
    <p>Compact countertop or undercounter Chewblet machines for lower-volume operations: office break rooms, small clinics, dental offices, executive suites. Chewblet ice is produced via extruded auger mechanism — water freezes on the inner drum surface, the auger continuously rotates scraping ice off, then compresses the scraped ice into nugget shape through an extrusion mechanism before discharge. When 7Series or 25Series production drops, the first diagnostic measurement is auger drive motor amp draw under load with a clamp meter. Elevated amps point to mechanical drag (worn auger flights at year 8-10, scale on drum interior, failing gear motor at year 5-8). Low or no amps point to motor windings or control circuit.</p>

    <h3 class="series-h3">Symphony Plus Healthcare Dispenser — dispense valve cycle observation</h3>
    <p>Hospital-grade ice and water dispensers with antimicrobial agitator, optional UV sanitization, and Follett's Sanitizer 2.0 cleaning cycle. Common at Cedars-Sinai, UCLA, Kaiser, and most LA-area dialysis centers. When Symphony Plus stops dispensing despite normal ice production, the most common cause is dispense valve actuator wear — the actuator cycles every time a patient or visitor operates the dispenser, hitting 200+ cycles per day on busy hospital floors. Diagnostic is direct observation: trigger a dispense cycle and watch for valve open-close response. Actuator replacement runs $245 to $385 with same-day restoration when stocked on the truck.</p>

    <h3 class="series-h3">Maestro Plus Restaurant Dispenser — combined diagnostic</h3>
    <p>Restaurant and beverage version of the Symphony platform. Same core mechanical architecture as Symphony Plus minus the healthcare-specific sanitization features. Common at higher-end LA restaurants, hotel pool bars, cocktail-focused operations where Chewblet ice is part of the menu specification. Diagnostic mirrors Symphony Plus (dispense valve, control board, water inlet, auger components) without the additional UV and Sanitizer 2.0 troubleshooting steps.</p>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="section">
  <div class="container narrow">
    <p class="section-number">Three-step diagnostic order</p>
    <h2>Cheapest tests first on every Follett no-production call.</h2>

    <p>Across LA County, OC, Ventura, and the Inland Empire, our techs run the same diagnostic order on every Follett no-production call — hospital floors at Cedars-Sinai, dialysis centers in Orange County, dental offices in Pasadena. We run cheapest tests first because the failure data backs it up: roughly 20% of calls clear at water supply confirmation, 60% require auger drive or dispense valve work (the Follett-dominant categories), and 20% require sealed-system or control board work.</p>

    <h3 class="series-h3">1. Water supply check (free, 5 minutes)</h3>
    <p>Walk to the supply line behind the Follett. Confirm the shut-off valve is fully open. Inspect supply tubing for kinks, crimps, or visible scale buildup. Check the water filter cartridge for overdue replacement. About 20% of calls clear here with no parts billed.</p>

    <h3 class="series-h3">2. Auger drive amp draw measurement (Chewblet) or dispense valve cycle (Symphony/Maestro)</h3>
    <p>The Follett-specific diagnostic step. On Chewblet 7Series, 25Series, and Ice Pro machines, measure auger drive motor amp draw under load with a clamp meter — elevated amps signal gear motor wear or upstream mechanical drag (auger flights, scale on drum). On Symphony Plus and Maestro Plus dispensers, trigger a dispense cycle and observe actuator response. Auger gear motor replacement runs $385 to $625; dispense valve actuator runs $245 to $385.</p>

    <h3 class="series-h3">3. Sealed-system or control board (last resort)</h3>
    <p>Last in the diagnostic order because it's the most expensive. Condenser fouling, refrigerant leak (EPA 608 leak detection plus brazed repair plus recharge $700 to $1,500), compressor failure ($1,200 to $2,400 depending on model), Symphony Plus control board end-of-life ($485 to $785). Our techs at Same Day Appliance Repair pre-confirm Follett parts availability at diagnostic so you have an accurate timeline before authorizing repair — less common Follett parts (older Symphony control boards, specialty Chewblet auger flights) can take 1 to 2 weeks on backorder.</p>
  </div>
</section>

